---
import Resumen from "../../layouts/Resumen.astro";
import { OPT_IN_TTL_MS } from "../../lib/subscriber/policy.ts";

const days = Math.round(OPT_IN_TTL_MS / (24 * 60 * 60_000));

/**
 * **The identical response**, and the whole of issue #61's third acceptance criterion.
 *
 * Four different things bring a subscriber here and the page cannot tell them apart, which is
 * the point: a brand-new address that has just been mailed a link, an address that is already
 * subscribed and has just been mailed another, an address inside its 24-hour cooldown that was
 * mailed nothing, and an address on the Do-Not-Contact list that will never be mailed again.
 * All four get this page, byte for byte.
 *
 * Every one of those is a fact about *the address*, which is why none of them may be spoken.
 * A form that said "you are already subscribed" would answer, for any address anyone cares
 * to type, whether its owner uses Pawster — and a form that said "that address reported us
 * as spam" would publish a complaint. The two refusals that *are* spoken, the per-IP limit
 * and the platform's daily ceiling, have pages of their own because neither is about the
 * address: one is about the caller and one is about us.
 *
 * So the words below have to be true of all four cases at once, which is why they say "if
 * it was you" and never "we sent you an email". The one they are least comfortable for is
 * Do-Not-Contact, and that discomfort is the correct trade: the alternative is telling a
 * stranger something about somebody else's inbox.
 */
---

<Resumen title="Revisa tu correo" heading="Revisa tu correo">
  <p data-testid="check-your-inbox">
    Si el correo que escribiste está bien y todo está en orden, te llega un mensaje con un
    enlace para activar tu búsqueda. Ábrelo y quedas listo.
  </p>

  <p>
    El enlace sirve una sola vez y vence en {days} días. Si no te llega en unos minutos,
    revisa la carpeta de spam y que el correo esté bien escrito.
  </p>

  <p data-testid="identical-response-notice">
    <!--
      The rule stated to the subscriber rather than only enforced, the same way
      `refugios/entrar/index.astro` states it to a shelter. Somebody who reads this page as
      confirmation and never receives mail would otherwise blame the platform; told that the
      page cannot know, they think to check the spelling.
    -->
    Esta página responde igual siempre, incluso si el correo ya estaba anotado o si escribiste
    uno que no es tuyo. Así nadie puede usar este formulario para averiguar quién recibe el
    resumen.
  </p>

  <p><a href="/resumen">Volver</a></p>
</Resumen>
